{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "rulesetVersion": "google-maps-en-2026.09.1",
  "minimumAppVersionCode": 1,
  "createdAt": "2026-07-12T00:00:00Z",
  "publisher": "PebbleNTN maintainers",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "google-maps-arrive-en",
      "enabled": true,
      "priority": 200,
      "packageNames": [
        "com.google.android.apps.maps"
      ],
      "locales": [
        "en"
      ],
      "comment": "Title only, and never the bare word 'arrive'. Google Maps puts the ETA in subText ('Arrive 23:51') on EVERY navigation notification, so matching combinedText here classified every turn as ARRIVE (real capture, 2026-07-13).",
      "conditions": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "operator": "regex",
          "value": "(?i)\\b(arriving|arrived|destination)\\b"
        }
      ],
      "output": {
        "maneuver": {
          "type": "literal",
          "value": "ARRIVE"
        },
        "primaryText": {
          "type": "firstNonEmpty",
          "fields": [
            "title",
            "text"
          ]
        },
        "secondaryText": {
          "type": "regexCapture",
          "field": "subText",
          "pattern": "(?i)\\barrive\\s+(\\d{1,2}:\\d{2}(?:\\s*[AaPp][Mm])?)",
          "group": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "google-maps-walk-arrive-in-en",
      "enabled": true,
      "priority": 195,
      "packageNames": [
        "com.google.android.apps.maps"
      ],
      "locales": [
        "en"
      ],
      "comment": "Walking, last stretch: ProgressStyle card, title 'Arrive in 1 min (70 m)', text '<destination>'. No turns remain, so ARRIVE with the distance to the destination; unmatched, the watch kept the last turn card ('0 m, turn right') for minutes (real capture, 2026-09). Just below google-maps-arrive-en, above every maneuver rule, so a destination name with a maneuver word cannot win. '1 min' never parses as a distance.",
      "conditions": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "operator": "regex",
          "value": "(?i)^\\s*arrive\\s+in\\s+\\d+\\s*min\\b"
        }
      ],
      "output": {
        "maneuver": {
          "type": "literal",
          "value": "ARRIVE"
        },
        "distanceMeters": {
          "type": "distance",
          "field": "title"
        },
        "primaryText": {
          "type": "firstNonEmpty",
          "fields": [
            "text",
            "title"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "google-maps-walk-overview-en",
      "enabled": true,
      "priority": 195,
      "packageNames": [
        "com.google.android.apps.maps"
      ],
      "locales": [
        "en"
      ],
      "comment": "Walking between turns: ProgressStyle card, title 'Walk 7 min (500 m)', text 'Arrive 18:57 · <destination>'. Continue toward the destination, with its ETA. Deliberately NO distance: the metres are the whole remaining walk, not the distance to the next turn, and under an arrow they would read as 'turn in 500 m' (real capture, 2026-09).",
      "conditions": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "operator": "regex",
          "value": "(?i)^\\s*walk\\s+\\d+\\s*min\\b"
        }
      ],
      "output": {
        "maneuver": {
          "type": "literal",
          "value": "STRAIGHT"
        },
        "primaryText": {
          "type": "regexCapture",
          "field": "text",
          "pattern": "·\\s*(.+?)\\s*$",
          "group": 1
        },
        "secondaryText": {
          "type": "regexCapture",
          "field": "text",
          "pattern": "(?i)\\barrive\\s+(\\d{1,2}:\\d{2}(?:\\s*[AaPp][Mm])?)",
          "group": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "google-maps-roundabout-distance-title-en",
      "enabled": true,
      "priority": 191,
      "packageNames": [
        "com.google.android.apps.maps"
      ],
      "locales": [
        "en"
      ],
      "comment": "Classic layout of google-maps-roundabout-en: title is the bare distance ('50 m'), text the instruction. Same maneuver, but the road line takes the instruction from text; the base rule's title-first primaryText showed the distance twice (real walking capture, 2026-09). One priority step above the base rule so it wins whenever the title is only a distance.",
      "conditions": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "operator": "regex",
          "value": "(?i)^\\s*\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?\\s*(?:km|m|mi|ft|yd)\\s*$"
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "operator": "regex",
          "value": "(?i)\\broundabout\\b"
        }
      ],
      "output": {
        "maneuver": {
          "type": "literal",
          "value": "ROUNDABOUT"
        },
        "distanceMeters": {
          "type": "distance",
          "field": "title"
        },
        "primaryText": {
          "type": "firstNonEmpty",
          "fields": [
            "text",
            "title"
          ]
        },
        "secondaryText": {
          "type": "regexCapture",
          "field": "subText",
          "pattern": "(?i)\\barrive\\s+(\\d{1,2}:\\d{2}(?:\\s*[AaPp][Mm])?)",
          "group": 1
        }
      }
    },
